    "created_at": "2022-01-21T11:28:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-01-21T11:28:58Z",
    "body": "I could imagine a collection of promises with a `get()` method that would return the same promise, depending on the arguments passed.\r\n\r\nSimilarly, I think we have cases where attributes can return a new promise after the corresponding object has undergone a (fundamental) state change.\r\n\r\nSo unfortunately I don't think there's a hard-and-fast rule here, but it's something to be looked at on a case-by-case basis.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
